{
  "id": "08702_nantonaku",
  "headword": "{何|なん}となく",
  "reading": "なんとなく",
  "part_of_speech": "adverb",
  "gloss": "somehow; vaguely; for some reason",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "somehow; vaguely; for some reason; without any particular reason",
      "explanation": "indicates an action or feeling that lacks a clear reason or cause"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "08702_nantonaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{何|なん}となく{気|き}になる。",
      "english": "It somehow bothers me.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08702_nantonaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{何|なん}となく{分|わ}かる{気|き}がする。",
      "english": "I feel like I vaguely understand.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08702_nantonaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{今日|きょう}は{何|なん}となく{外|そと}に{出|で}たくない{気分|きぶん}だ。",
      "english": "Today I don't feel like going out for some reason.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "STRUCTURE:\n{何|なん}と (what) + なく (without) → \"without [being/doing] anything particular\"\n\nUSAGE:\nDescribes vague feelings, impressions, or actions without a specific reason:\n- {何|なん}となく{分|わ}かる - I vaguely understand\n- {何|なん}となく{好|す}き - I kind of like it\n- {何|なん}となく{嫌|いや}な{予感|よかん} - a vague bad feeling\n\nNUANCE:\nConveys uncertainty or lack of clear reasoning. Often used when describing intuitions, impressions, or feelings that are hard to articulate.\n\nSIMILAR EXPRESSIONS:\n- どことなく - somehow, vaguely (often for appearances/atmosphere)\n- なぜか - for some reason (stronger sense of mystery)\n- {漠然|ばくぜん}と - vaguely (more formal)",
